# Day 16

**26km / 6.5 hours**

An interesting day which began with some pleasant coastal walking. This involved some pleasant coastal areas including a short walk to see a monument commemorating an old ship disaster in the area, this was notable for having a nice lookout of the surrounding coasts.

![A very long bridge to start the walk today](./long-bridge.jpg)

![The coasts from the memorial point](./coasts.jpg)

After that pleasant experience and passing some nice beaches it was back to the road. Again there's not a huge amount to say about this but it was a long stretch of the day so I feel I have to mention it. There was a bit where the road went into the forest for the cycling path which was a bit nicer but there wasn't much until we got to the town of Ngunguru. Then it was just a matter of getting a boat across the river, although we ended up swimming which was enjoyable. The boat just took our packs over.